{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And YHWH said to Aharon: You and your sons, etc. — ״וְזָר לֹא יִקְרַב״ — ״וְהַזָּר הַקָּרֵב יוּמָת״ — behold, I have warned them with the penalty of death. Henceforth there is no need for concern [about the doubling in] ״הַקָּרֵב… יִקְרַב״ — for I have already forbidden them with ״לֹא יִקְרַב״, and I have made them liable to death."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The lemma phrases are drawn from Numbers 18:1, 18:4, and 18:7 respectively; Rashbam cites them sequentially without addresses. The expression אין לחוש הקרב הקרב refers to the rhetorical question of why Scripture uses both a prohibition (לא יקרב) and a positive death-penalty statement (והזר הקרב יומת) for the same act of unauthorized approach."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:47.097288548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}